  "notes": "Source: official UCF Barry S. Miller College of Business Management degree page, https://business.ucf.edu/degree/management/ , 'Curricular Plan of Study' section, fetched and transcribed verbatim 2026-09-30. The page carries no printed catalog-year label; it is the currently published plan (page crawled live 2026-09-30) and is labeled 2026-2027 as the current catalog cycle. Transcription method: manual course-by-course transcription of the plan's Freshman/Sophomore/Junior/Senior term lists; titles use the page's wording. CAVEATS: (1) The live page's Senior Spring list includes a duplicated 'ACG 2021 Principles of Financial Accounting' row (identical to the Sophomore Fall course) - an apparent CMS copy-paste error. Six listed items would sum to 16 credits against the page's own '(13 hours)' header, so the duplicate row is EXCLUDED here; the remaining five rows sum to the header's 13 hours. (2) Page prints 'MAN 3301 Strategic Huan Resource Management' (typo); corrected to the official catalog title 'Strategic Human Resource Management'. (3) Junior Spring lists 'QMB 3602' with no title on this page; title 'Business Research for Decision Making' taken from the same official site's accounting degree page (business.ucf.edu/degree/accounting/). (4) The page's term-hour headers (15+15+15+15+15+13+16+13) sum to 117, not 120. GEB 3006 Career Development & Financial Planning (1 cr, required before beginning any business major per the same page) is named only in a Junior Fall milestone and is not placed in any term list, so it is not transcribed as a term slot. The UCF degree requirement is a minimum 120 unduplicated semester hours; remaining hours beyond the 117-term plan are earned via additional general electives (the UCF catalog print notes 'General electives as required to earn 120 credit hours'). (5) Business-core courses are categorized as 'major' (schema has no 'core' category). (6) prereq arrays are left empty: the plan page does not list per-course prerequisites. (7) GEP/ELECT/MAJOREL are placeholder codes for student-choice slots (choice:true) per the page's 'Foundation'/'General Elective'/'Management Elective' rows; all other rows are fixed courses with distinct codes.",
